-- echo: the minimal module for the §13.13 import tests. Every atom in
-- here is namespaced by the importer's suffix (Echo_v2, Echoed_v2, …);
-- the module replies into whatever bag the caller passes as DATA —
-- a module cannot name the real Global (its mention of it would be
-- mangled too); the caller shapes what happens next (§4 continuations).
(Echo, m, reply) : lob reply (Echoed, m)

(Announce, reply) : lob reply (Announced,)

-- The boot witness: a one-shot declared in its own bag, so the
-- importer's hide list can skip it. Fires once when the module is
-- spawned, out'ing into the module's own (mangled) Boot bag.
Boot {
  : (Booted,)
}
